Found under k273 (2026-10-31). The GPU Operator step's nvidia.com/gpu allocatable wait covers the NVIDIA nodes it detects at that moment. A worker that joins later in the same `ocp apply` is only re-checked (setup_gpu_operator_after_join) when the first GPU Operator check skipped, so its allocatable is not waited for until the next apply.

Done = decide whether after_join should also wait for newly joined NVIDIA nodes when the first check ran (mirror AMDGPU::after_join), test it, or record why not.

